so i was thinking that it's sort of strange that, given that golems
are magical constructs designed to essentially be pets, there's no way
for the player to create a loyal one themselves.

one idea would be a new spell "create golem". it would be directional
and would have to be cast towards a pile of items sufficiently large
as to generate a golem if it were polymorphed. this spell would
usually create a tame golem though perhaps occassionally a hostile one
to introduce a little risk. probably this should be about the same
level as create familiar. Or maybe it could be quite low level but,
drawing from the many golem-related cautionary tales in myth, the
golem could have a chance of randomly turning hostile (skipping over
peaceful) every few hundred turns.

the other idea would be to latch into the already existing polymorph
wand/spell code and just make generated golems have a chance of being
tame (perhaps only if all the items used to make them were blessed?).
this could also be a nice little perk if polypiling is going to be
reduced in utility some (which i seem to remember being talked about
in IRC quite a while ago).

